  "id": "DrugBank_DB01262 - MONDO_5224",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Decitabine and Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia Without Maturation (AMLWM) through a chain of indications involving Ivosidenib. Decitabine is associated with Unclassified Acute Myeloid Leukemia and Therapy Related Acute Myeloid Leukemia And Myelodysplastic Syndrome, both of which are linked to Ivosidenib. Ivosidenib, in turn, is indicated for AMLWM. This suggests that Decitabine may be indirectly linked to AMLWM through its association with other leukemias that are targeted by Ivosidenib. The scores of 0.7146 indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship. The mechanism appears to involve shared pathways or therapeutic targets, though the exact nature of the interaction remains unclear. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, but further research is needed to confirm the direct relationship between Decitabine and AMLWM.",
